The Analogy: Riding a City Bus. The route is fixed, the driver is hired, and the mechanics maintain the vehicle. You buy a ticket, step in, and use the service as a passenger.

What You Get: A fully finished, functional software application accessible via a web browser or mobile app.

Who Manages What:

Provider handles: Everything (hardware, OS, code updates, security patches, backend databases, and backups).

You handle: Your own account settings and your personal data.

Real-World Examples:

Google Workspace (Gmail, Google Docs, Drive)

Zoom / Microsoft Teams

Netflix / Spotify
